# Starter CODEOWNERS for the open-contribution practice.
# Replace <owner> (a team like @org/platform in a real org, not an individual) and the
# example paths with this repo's law files, then delete lines that do not apply.
#
# The idea: anyone can touch these files; merging them requires the owner. Keep the list
# short enough to recite - protection that covers everything protects nothing, it just
# makes the owner the bottleneck.

# Plans and billing - a wrong merge here charges someone money.
# /src/billing/                 <owner>
# /src/plans/                   <owner>

# Tenancy - a wrong merge here shows someone else's data.
# /src/tenancy/                 <owner>

# The LLM chokepoint - every model call flows through it; changes need tests, always.
# /src/llm/                     <owner>

# Agent law - what every agent in the repo obeys.
# /.claude/                     <owner>
# /CLAUDE.md                    <owner>
# /AGENTS.md                    <owner>

# CI workflows - the gate itself.
# /.github/workflows/           <owner>
